Reading photo text as OCR words instead of pixels is far worse, so that idea is closed. Two of the three cells stuck in the queue were moved to a second partition, and one of them is now running. Nothing needed from you.

## Done this wake
- **TextVQA as OCR text, seed 42 (decided).** I gave the model the OCR words instead of the image, on 500 TextVQA questions. Each answer was compared with the pixel answer to the same question:

  | input | questions | judge accuracy ↑ | difference (95% CI) | slots per question |
  |---|---|---|---|---|
  | pixels (baseline) | 500 | .780 | — | 54.2 |
  | OCR text | 500 | .346 | −.434 [−.480, −.384], 17 better / 234 worse, McNemar p = 6e-50 | 4.4 (.081× of pixels) |

  - The gold answer appears in the OCR words on only 59.6% of questions, which is below what the pixels already score.
  - So the photo-text loss is not an OCR-reading problem. No "pixels plus OCR" run is motivated (the bar was a gain of at least 5 points).
- **Queue fix.** Three cells had waited 6.5–7 hours on `gpu-be` (the best-effort partition, where running jobs can be stopped). SLURM's start estimates ran as far out as 18 November. The campaign rules allow moving at most 2 cells to `gpu,gpu-be` after 6 hours.
  - I moved the two cells that each settle a result at both seeds.
  - The evidence-then-answer repeat started within a minute.
  - The other moved cell's estimate went from 18 November to 14:49 today.
- **Results page.** `docs/probe_campaign_2026-11.md` now has the new status, a new finding (#8), a table for this result and an updated "Closed" list. `STATE.md` and the campaign rules are updated to match.

## Running now
| what it tests | state |
|---|---|
| Copy the evidence, then answer (seed 43). This repeats a tie seen at seed 42 | running on `gpu`, which cannot be preempted; ends about 08:20 |
| Keep only the most-attended quarter of the slots (seed 43) | waiting, estimate 14:49 |
| Keep only an eighth of the slots (seed 42) | waiting on `gpu-be`, estimate 16:30 |

## Budget and next wake
- 64 of 65 cells are used. The last one is kept for a single relaunch if a cell fails its health check.
- The loop wakes when the evidence-then-answer cell finishes, or when both slot-pruning cells have, or after 12 hours at most.
